<title>USA: Weekend box office chart - Oct 4-6.</title>
<headline>Weekend box office chart - Oct 4-6.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office during the Friday to Sunday weekend, according to studio estimates released by Exhibitor Relations Co. Final data will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>(Last weekend's position in parenthesis, * = new release).</p>
<p>    1 (1) First Wives Club ................. $11.1 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) The Glimmer Man ..................  $7.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (*) That Thing You Do! ...............  $6.6 million</p>
<p>    4 (*) D3. The Mighty Ducks .............  $6.55 million</p>
<p>    5 (2) Extreme Measures .................  $4.1 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) 2 Days in the Valley .............  $2.3 million</p>
<p>    7 (3) Last Man Standing ................  $2.2 million</p>
<p>    8 (5) Fly Away Home ....................  $2.1 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) Independence Day .................. $1.4 million</p>
<p>   10(16) Big Night ........................  $1.2 million</p>
<p>NOTE: First Wives Club is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.. &quot;The Glimmer Man&quot; is released by Time Warner Inc.'s Warner Bros. &quot;That Thing You Do!&quot; and &quot;Independence Day&quot; are released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;D3: The Mighty Ducks&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co.. &quot;Extreme Measures&quot; and &quot;Fly Away Home&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp. &quot;2 Days in the Valley&quot; is released by MGM, which is being bought by a consortium backed by investor Kirk Kerkorian. &quot;Last Man Standing&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Turner Broadcasting System Inc.. &quot;Big Night&quot; is released by Orion Pictures, a unit of Metromedia International Group Inc.</p>
</text>
